  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Phụ âm · Consonants",
     "texto": [
      "In this chapter we look at four consonants and three letter groups: seven sounds in total.",
      "**q** (always written **qu**): in the north, like the «qu» in «quick»; in the south, more like a soft «gw»: «guái».",
      "**s**: in the north, like a normal «s»; in the south, with the tongue slightly further back (almost like the English «sh»).",
      "**t**: somewhere between English «t» and «d», with no puff of air, like the «t» in «stop».",
      "**v**: like the English «v» (the upper teeth on the lower lip). In the south it sometimes sounds like a «y».",
      "**nh**: like the **ny** in «canyon»: nhà ≈ «nyah».",
      "**ph**: like an English **f**: phở ≈ «fuh».",
      "**tr**: in the north, like the English «ch» in «church»; in the south, like a «ch» with the tongue further back (almost like the English «tr»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Nguyên âm · Vowels that end in -i / -y",
     "texto": [
      "These combinations only appear at the **end** of the syllable: no other consonant ever comes after them.",
      "**ai**: like the «i» in «eye», but longer (the a lasts longer).",
      "**ay**: also «ai», but the a is **short** and the i comes straight away.",
      "**ây**: like «ay» in «day», even shorter than **ay**: bây giờ ≈ «bay zuh».",
      "**ui**: like «ooey» in «gooey».",
      "**uy**: a closer «ui», almost like the English word «we»: quý ≈ «kwee».",
      "**oi**: a very open «o» followed by an i, long.",
      "**ôi**: «oi» like in «boy»: tôi ≈ «toy».",
      "**Tip:** the ones that end in **-y** are shorter than the ones that end in **-i**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
